# Features in Gherkin

When a user-visible behavior is added or changed, update a scenario under `features/`. Gherkin is the UX reference. Do not add Cucumber, step definitions, or CI for these files unless asked.

## Shape

- One `features/<name>.feature` per area (`review.feature`, `diff.feature`)
- `Feature`, `Scenario`, and `Given` / `When` / `Then` in plain English
- Name the screen, file, and outcome the user sees
- Keep an existing scenario and edit it when the behavior changes
- Remove a scenario when the behavior is removed

```gherkin
Feature: Review comments

  Scenario: Copy a line comment for an agent
    Given a diff of "src/app.rb"
    When I comment on line 1
    And I copy reviews
    Then the clipboard contains "`src/app.rb:1`"
```
